Z||000001||deceler8||01-03-2001||11:55 AM||||Knock at low RPM's is probably due to low oil pressure at idle. <P>But a similar condition could exist if a cylinder isn't getting spark. The powerless cylinder could make a noise that might seem like a knock.<P>As to your "disconnect wires" problem...don't have a clue.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||01-03-2001||12:02 PM||||<BR>Since your purchase of the Fiero have you done a tune-up to it.  Replacement of plugs, wires, dist. cap and rotor?  If not, do so and that <I>weird situation</I> may go away.<P>Feeding off of deceler8's low oil pressure statemnt, the oil pressure sending unit may be bad or the oil pump itself may be gone.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Matt88||01-03-2001||04:04 PM||||You've probably checked this at least 1,000 times already - but, make sure you put the plug wires back on correctly.  You usually know right away if you put the wrong wire on the sparkplug (like #1 on #3), but if the engine is worn enough, the incorrect order can cause nothing more than a knock.  Also, have you checked your initial timing?  If the tuneup was long overdue, the timing can be way advanced or retarded.  <P>Keep in mind your engine is probably knocking at higher rpm - you just can't hear it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||01-03-2001||04:14 PM||||I'd agree with Matt on this one, new spark plug wires, old wire can 'bleed' and cause cylinders to fire at the wrong time. Also, the timing thing makes sence, and it only costs like $30 to have a shop check it. But if neither of those fix it, it could be a weak oil pump or a spun bearing. do you have an oil preasure guage, or just the light? if your warm oil preasure while driving is low, like below 40, and your idle preasure is below 10, it's mostlikely a rod bearing. The timing and wires is going to be your easiest/cheapest things to check.||||reg||1
